{"id": "EUVD-2026-97698", "enisaUuid": "f618f4b6-2f36-3382-96b2-0f0a570f55f3", "description": "FreeRDP 2.1.0 before 3.32.0 contains a use-after-free vulnerability in the static rdpsnd channel disconnect path, which frees audio formats and device without joining play_thread. A malicious RDP server can disconnect while asynchronous Wave2 playback processes queued PDUs, causing the client to read freed heap memory and crash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:56:42", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-vqxm-9w7c-hvvx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.1.0-before-3.32.0-use-after-free-via-rdpsnd-disconnect-path"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109254", "GHSA-qmqf-2qmq-qw2p"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5f431dc3-cb23-3b5d-8e3c-5659de48f9bb", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.1.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "66c8dab1-ed0e-3d01-ab18-92a992fba949", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}